			"notes": "## Additions\n- Added full support for 26.3\n  - New jar! Mojang rewrote the interpolation code again!\n- Added `applyVelocityForInterpolated` setting\n  - If disabled, entities with interpolation will not have velocity applied client-side\n  - Enabled by default, though it may cause jittering for interpolated entities in 26.3.\n- Added a partial fix for [MC-311974](https://mojira.dev/MC-311974)\n  - In technical detail, the `updateInterval() + 1`, `advance()` movement and `currentStepTicks = 1.0F -> 0.0F` fixes have been implemented\n  - The rest of the issues with the new stepped interpolation handler remain as Anti-Smooth simply just resorts to the old linear interpolation handler for entities that have update packets sent every tick.  \n\n## Changes\n- Reworked the `unaffectedEntities` setting\n  - The default value is now an empty list\n  - The former default value of this setting is now a hardcoded list\n  - This new list can be disabled with the `disableDefaultUnaffectedEntities` setting\n- The `applyVelocity` setting now only applies when the affected mob is not being interpolated\n\n## Bug Fixes\n- Fixed interpolation steps in 1.21.5+ always being set to 1 regardless of settings\n- Fixed interpolation conditions being really messy"
		},
